  "diagnosis": "The construction is faithful (RMS 0.48 meV over the target states) and every generic check passes. dmft_subspace_model_window fails only for structural reasons: the automatic PDWF pass kept every pseudo-atomic orbital. On Ni that is d1 (3d) plus s2 and p2 (4s and 4p); on O it is 2s and 2p. That gives 26 functions per spin against the target's 16 (Ni 3d \u00d72, O 2p \u00d72), and the extra Ni 4s/4p and O 2s orbitals are not target seeds. The repair keeps only Ni d1 and O 2p. O 2s (bands 9-10, isolated 10.6 eV below the O 2p bands) moves into the bottom exclusion, which the gate accepts. dis_froz_max is lowered so the frozen window holds no more than 16 states: at +2.26 eV it held 17 at \u0393 in spin 1, the extra one being band 27 (the band above the target), which starts at 1.535 eV.",
